*bundles* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

''combine'' can create bundles containing program code, plugins, and assets.
These bundles execute like normal programs with automatic extraction at runtime.

The binary bundle format is specific to ChipLang and is called ''CHIPBIN''.

''combine'' can also produce text bundles that are not encased in a binary.
See ''chippy doc combine'', specifically ''ProduceBundle''.

*Bundle Commands:*
- ''chippy bundle show <file>'' - Display bundle metadata
- ''chippy bundle extract <file>'' - Extract bundle to directory

See ''chippy doc combine'' for bundle creation.

*In Your Program:*

''libbundle.chh'' helps with common bundle related tasks in your programs (such as accessing files)
See ''chippy doc /usr/lib/chiplang/libbundle.chh''.

*Bundle Constants:*

These are always available.

- ''BUNDLERUN'': Set to ''true'' when running from a bundle, ''false'' otherwise
- ''BUNDLEDIR'': String path to extraction directory, ''err'' if not running in a bundle
- ''BUNDLEID'': Bundle ID, ''null'' if not running in a bundle

See ''chippy doc chipbin'' for the binary format specification.
